<title>BELGIUM: Barry-Callebaut merger approved in Belgium - report.</title>
<headline>Barry-Callebaut merger approved in Belgium - report.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Belgian appeals court has approved the merger of the Belgian operations of chocolate firms Cacao Barry SA and Callebaut AG, overturning a decision by Belgium's anti-trust watchdog to block the deal, Belga news agency reported.</p>
<p>The anti-trust body, the Competition Council, had argued the combination of Barry with Callebaut, a unit of Swiss chocolate group Klaus J.Jacobs Holding, would distort the market for chocolate casings used by Belgium's praline industry.</p>
<p>The court's decision is backdated to November 25, 1996, the date of the original merger, Belga said.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
